+# 🌉 Bridge Work Order — [P2] Tools suite absent: no Translate / Mindmap / Doc export / Calendar / Podcast / Form surfaces anywhere in the product (Monica Gap 4/8) (bridge-20261027-audit-gap-tools-suite)
+
+## Problem
+The Bangla feature audit (2026-10-27) mapped Monica's tools suite (Translate, Calendar, Doc, Mindmap, Podcast, Form) as Gap 4 and found it completely absent: SupremeAI ships zero user-facing tool surfaces. The audit's exact verdict for this row: fully missing — no user-facing tool surface exists.
+
+Everything needed to power these tools is already in production: the provider gateway routes chat-completion traffic across healthy providers (51/51 keys at last check), streaming works end to end in Studio, and the frontend has route-level infrastructure. A translation tool is a streaming completion with a system prompt and a language pair; a mindmap tool is an outline completion rendered as a tree; a doc export is a chat thread reformatted into a document. None of these needs a new provider, new key, or new backend subsystem — they need surfaces.
+
+Retention reality: tools are the daily-utility hook. Chat alone competes with every general assistant; a fast Translate and a one-click Mindmap give users a reason to open the product on days when they do not have a "question". Monica's suite exists precisely for this.
+
+## Impact
+- Retention: no daily-utility surface means no habitual opening pattern.
+- Home-market fit: Bengali↔English translation quality is a showcase capability for the primary market, and it is currently invisible.
+- Output value: users cannot take anything structured (mindmap, document) out of the product; every conversation dies in the scrollback.
+
+## Fix (smallest safe change) — wave 1, top 3 by audit value ranking
+1. **Translate**: paste or upload text, language pair selector (wave 1: Bengali↔English plus one more pair), streaming output, copy button. One API endpoint wrapping the existing chat route with a translation system prompt.
+2. **Mindmap**: text/outline input → markdown-outline completion → rendered interactive tree; export as PNG/SVG. Renderer is frontend-only over the generated outline.
+3. **Doc export**: select a chat thread → generate formatted document (headings, code blocks preserved) → download as Markdown and DOCX. Reuses existing document-generation capability server-side if present, else template-based rendering.
+
+Each tool is one Studio route + one thin API endpoint; all lazy-loaded. Calendar, Podcast and Form are explicitly deferred to wave 2 — one cohesive small wave at a time (P7 sizing discipline: 30 files / 200 KB ceiling).
+
+## Acceptance Criteria
+- [ ] Translate works for Bengali↔English with streaming output; complex-script shaping renders correctly (home-market check)
+- [ ] Mindmap renders a ≥3-level tree from an outline; PNG export produces a usable image
+- [ ] Doc export produces a .docx and a .md from a real chat thread with headings and code blocks preserved
+- [ ] Each tool is lazy-loaded; initial route JS budget does not regress
+- [ ] Each tool call flows through the provider gateway (health routing + rate limit apply), no direct provider calls from the frontend
+
+## Reflection Evidence (why + alternatives_rejected)
+**Why:** tools are the cheapest retention surface and the audit ranked Translate/Mindmap/Doc as the highest-value first wave; all three are compositions of capabilities that already run in production.
+**Alternatives rejected:** (a) building all six tools in one order — violates cohesive sizing and delays shipping the wave that matters; (b) embedding third-party tool iframes — breaks the data boundary, adds external dependencies, and imports someone else's outage and brand; (c) starting with Podcast — highest cost, narrowest audience.
+
+## Labels
+`bridge:queued` `P2-medium` `area:studio` `gap:monica-04`
